        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>ARPAD</strong> (Isaiah 10:9; 36:19; 37:13), also Arphad, support, a Syrian city near Hamath, along with which it is invariably mentioned (2 Kings 19:13; 18:34; Isaiah 10:9), and Damascus (Jeremiah 49:23). After a siege of three years it fell (B.C. 742) before the Assyrian king Tiglath-pileser II. Now Tell Erfud.",
        "Easton's Illustrated Bible Dictionary, M. G. Easton (1897). Public domain.",
